## TaggerView

- Baseline is the live catalog row (DECKS and MOVE_TIMESTAMPS). Compare parsed names, players, and timestamps (padded with null), not JSON text.
- Restore in the SET_DECK effect. If a stored draft parses, parseTimestampsJson with the draft's own timestamp count. SET_DECK with that count and the draft's own names and players, then LOAD those timestamps. Do not use applyJsonToMachine.
- If the stored text does not parse, SET_DECK from the catalog and put the stored text back in the textarea so the load error shows.
- After the deck-change history reset, set jsonDraft from the stored text when present.
- When jsonDraft is non-empty, save it for the current deck, or clear the key when the parsed document matches the baseline. Skip the empty string. Skip a write whose parsed deckId is not the deck on screen.
- On a successful Save, patch that deck in the in-memory catalog from the JSON just sent, then clear its local draft.
- resetTimestamps sends SET_DECK with the catalog count, names, and players, then RESET with catalog timestamps, then clears the JSON draft. Confirm copy says the catalog.

Undo/redo stays session-only.

